    {
      "bbox": [
        677,
        748,
        2355,
        1747
      ],
      "category": "Text",
      "text": "With respect to elected officials, however, their right to participate in politics as party officers or otherwise should in no way be restricted. They are chosen by the electorate with the expectation that they will pursue the policies which they have advocated in their political campaigns and their actions are subject to review by their constitutency whenever they seek elective office. As an elected official, the Mayor is expected to carry out political objectives and he should not be limited in his selection of personal aids on an executive level, such as the Deputy Mayors and Assistants to the Mayor.",
